#---
# purpose: "a receive clause may name a tuple arity the module never constructs"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# # receive_unconstructed_tuple_arity
#
# A receive clause naming a tuple arity that nothing in the module builds is a
# clause no message can match. It is still a legal clause, and it compiles to
# that answer on every door.
#
# The module here constructs only a 2-tuple, so no 4-tuple schema is ever
# registered. The receive matcher's arity question for the `{:b, p, q, r}`
# clause therefore has no schema id to compare against, and the right answer is
# false: no value in this program can carry a schema that was never minted.
#
# Before the receive matcher asked its arity question through
# `RuntimeTypePredicate`, the native door raised a codegen error on the missing
# registration instead. The interpreter answered false and printed 1, so this
# shape failed to compile on `run` and `build` while succeeding on `interp`.
def main() do
  send(self(), {:a, 1})

  x = receive do
    {:a, n} -> n
    {:b, p, q, r} -> p + q + r
  end

  dbg(x)
end
